  "worked_solution": "For the two lines to be perpendicular, their slopes must multiply to $-1.$\n\nTo find the slope of $10x+5y=3,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10x+5y & =3 \\\\ 5y & =-10x+3 \\\\ y & =-2x+\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the slope of $2kx+y=2,$ we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2kx+y & =2 \\\\ y & =-2kx+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- The slope of the line $10x+5y=3$ is $-2.$\n\n- The slope of the line $2kx+y=2$ is $-2k.$\n\nMultiplying the slopes together, we have\n\n$$\n(-2)\\cdot (-2k)=-1\\,\u27f9\\,k=-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
